      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 27,
        "relationship_type": "antonym",
        "body": "好き and 嫌い are な-Adjectives used to express 'like' and 'dislike.' The object of like or dislike is typically marked with が, though を can appear in some cases. Adding 大 (e.g., 大好き, 大嫌い) intensifies the sentiment, transforming 'like' and 'dislike' into something more akin to 'love' and 'hate.'",
